This is my first journal entry. From now on, every reflection I add will be a new file in the
`_posts` folder, named with the date first.

## What I worked on today

- Set up this static website with Jekyll and GitHub Pages.
- Wrote down my long-term goals on the Goals page.

## Progress toward my goals

- **Goal 1:** Created a place to record consistent reflections over time.

## What was hard

- Understanding how Jekyll turns Markdown files into a finished website.

## What I learned

- A static site has no database: I add a new Markdown file, commit it, and the site rebuilds
  itself automatically.

## Next step

- Write one short reflection after each major project or study milestone.
